  "verbalization": "Eprosartan is linked to Hypertensive Disorder through a chain of off-label use and indications. The evidence suggests that Eprosartan, when used off-label, is associated with Diabetic Nephropathy, which in turn is linked to other drugs that are used to treat hypertension. Specifically, Eprosartan is off-label used for Diabetic Nephropathy, and this condition is indicated for Captopril and Irbesartan, both of which are used to manage hypertension. The shared pathway from Eprosartan to Diabetic Nephropathy and then to Hypertensive Disorder highlights a potential mechanism where off-label use of Eprosartan may contribute to the development of hypertension through its effects on kidney function. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of off-label use in linking Eprosartan to hypertension, emphasizing the importance of considering off-label indications in drug repurposing.",
